Task: Multi-axis range parsing and joint candidate grid

Changes:
- CMC now accepts legacy (lo, hi) or a sequence of per-axis pairs.
- Per-axis resolution (int broadcast or sequence), validated against arity.
- optimize_over normalization (default: first two ICPs) and grid-size cap
  (MAX_GRID_POINTS=1,000,000) checked before allocation.
- candidate_grid() builds the Cartesian product with meshgrid(indexing='ij'),
  whose ravel order is lexicographic for ascending axes.
- Legacy 1-D mitigate path adapted to the normalized ranges/resolutions.

Tests: legacy 1-D range, 2-D product ordering, per-axis resolution, and
invalid configurations (missing/duplicate range, lo>hi, wrong arity, res<2).

Files: surrogate_xapps/cmc.py, tests/test_cmc.py
